The drawing stage now uses a local embedded qualityrender module when no existing
renderer URL is configured. The worker renders HTML/SVG in offline Chromium and
runs the supplied best.pt model (Ultralytics 8.4.14) on sampled frames, returning
PNG/WebP and the real normal/unnormal verdict. Existing renderer settings are not
rewritten. Manual quality runs return immediately and persist total, completed,
running, queued, current account, current stage, and elapsed per-account phase.
The missing renderer configuration path is removed from normal operation: the main website image embeds the worker and best.pt classifier. Existing non-empty renderer URLs are still honored unchanged.
Final remote state preserves the original postgres:18-alpine base and leaves existing Compose/environment settings untouched.
